AR(1)                       User Commands                    AR(1)

NAME
    ar - maintain archives of files

SYNOPSIS
    ar [-]{dpqrtx}[cousv] archive [member...]

DESCRIPTION
    ar creates and modifies archives in the System V format. One operation
    letter is required. Without member names t, p and x act on every member.

OPERATIONS
    d   delete the named members
    p   print the named members to standard output
    q   append the files without checking for duplicates
    r   add the files, replacing members of the same name in place
    t   list the members
    x   extract the named members into the current directory

MODIFIERS
    c   do not report the creation of a new archive
    o   set the modification time of extracted files from the archive
    u   with r, replace a member only when the file is newer
    s   accepted; no symbol table is written
    v   verbose: a, r, d and x lines for added, replaced, deleted and
        extracted members; mode, owner, size, date and name for t

EXAMPLES
    ar rc libm.a a.o b.o
    ar tv libm.a
    ar x libm.a a.o

SEE ALSO
    make(1), tar(1)
